# service map (checked in deck XML): three blue connectors leave the SI. One is bound to the License app.
# One runs straight behind the Archive app to its Windows Server. One is an elbow that crosses between
# the SQL DB and Archive app (it looks like an Archive->SQL link in the image) and runs down behind the
# SQL DB to its Windows Server. Read as SI -> each app CI -> its server, as on the Run slide (47).
pdm-prod -> sql-db
pdm-prod -> archive-app
pdm-prod -> license-app
sql-db -> win-sql
archive-app -> win-archive
license-app -> win-license
# slide draws one blue line from the router through all three servers
router -> win-sql
router -> win-archive
router -> win-license

db-admin-so -> sql-db
db-admin-so -> db-admin
win-servers -> win-sql
win-servers -> win-archive
win-servers -> win-license
net-routers -> router
net-routers -> switch
network-admin -> net-routers
network-admin -> network-services
windows-admin -> win-servers
windows-admin -> compute

# strategic (purple): Manage Technology provided by the four TMS along the left-hand line. In the deck XML the
# connectors are chained (Manage Technology -> DB Admin, Network Services -> DB Admin, Network Services -> Compute);
# App Mgmt is not bound but the line runs through it. Modelled as the BC provided by all four.
manage-tech -> app-mgmt
manage-tech -> db-admin
manage-tech -> network-services
manage-tech -> compute
